# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values once you've signed up for Twilio.
# .env is gitignored — never commit real credentials.
#
# What you need to get, and from where:
#
# 1. Create a Twilio account at https://www.twilio.com/try-twilio
#    (requires a payment method on file — Claude did NOT do this, by design)
#
# 2. From the Twilio Console dashboard (https://console.twilio.com), copy:
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=ACxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your_auth_token_here
#
# 3. Buy a phone number (Console -> Phone Numbers -> Buy a number).
#    Needs Voice capability. Paste it in E.164 format:
TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=+1xxxxxxxxxx
#
# 4. Your own number, so outbound calls know who to dial and inbound calls
#    can be restricted to just you:
JARVIS_OWNER_PHONE_NUMBER=+1xxxxxxxxxx
#
# 5. Twilio needs a PUBLIC https URL to reach twilio_server.py's webhooks.
#    For local dev, run ngrok (https://ngrok.com, has a free tier):
#      ngrok http 5005
#    then paste the https URL it gives you here (no trailing slash):
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://your-ngrok-subdomain.ngrok-free.app
#
# 6. In the Twilio Console, set your phone number's "A call comes in" webhook
#    (Voice -> your number -> Voice Configuration) to:
#      {PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/voice
#    method POST. That's the only Twilio-side config needed beyond buying
#    the number.
